Adapted source:
  src/filter/beauty_face_unit_filter.cc
  src/core/gpupixel_framebuffer.cc (GL_LINEAR / GL_CLAMP_TO_EDGE semantics)
  src/source/source_image.cc (unflipped RGBA upload semantics)

Unmodified LUT pixel data, losslessly embedded as RGB bytes:
  src/res/lookup_gray.png   (256 x 1)
  src/res/lookup_origin.png (64 x 64)
  src/res/lookup_skin.png   (64 x 64)
  src/res/lookup_light.png  (512 x 512)

MaiPortraitWhiteningLutData.inc records each original PNG SHA-256 and its decoded
RGB SHA-256. tests/generate-whitening-lut-data.py reproduces the file with Pillow.
The Paeth predictor, canonical Huffman coding and base64 wrapping only compress
storage; they do not resample, approximate, retrain or otherwise change the LUTs.
The CPU module has no runtime Pillow, platform image loader, GL or zlib dependency.

Adaptation notes:
- The public argument is the shader whiten uniform in [0, 1]. Upstream's macOS
  SetWhite divides its API argument by ten; there is no such division here.
  Shader .25 therefore corresponds to upstream macOS API 2.5.
- At zero, the upstream shader bypasses every whitening stage. Every positive
  value first applies levels, gray, origin and skin stages, then interpolates
  skin -> light with the supplied uniform. This preserves its discontinuity at
  zero; a tiny positive value does not approach the unedited source.
- Alpha is preserved, matching the GLES shader and the RGBA8 host contract. The
  upstream desktop GL shader instead writes constant alpha 1.0.
- CPU float bilinear LUT sampling follows normalized GL_LINEAR coordinates and
  GL_CLAMP_TO_EDGE. GPU interpolation and final RGBA8 rounding may differ by a
  least-significant byte; validate against pinned GPU outputs with that tolerance.
- This pointwise module does not identify skin or select subjects. Its caller
  controls selection, spatial masks and compositing in original-image space.
